## Repository Management

### Remote Management
```bash
# View remotes
git remote -v

# Add remote
git remote add origin https://github.com/ibucketbranch/AgentSaasy_NGAI.git

# Change remote URL
git remote set-url origin <new-url>

# Remove remote
git remote remove origin
```

### Tagging Releases
```bash
# Create annotated tag
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release version 1.0.0"

# Push tags
git push origin v1.0.0

# Push all tags
git push origin --tags

# List tags
git tag
```

### Cleaning Up
```bash
# Delete local branch
git branch -d feature/old-feature

# Delete remote branch
git push origin --delete feature/old-feature

# Prune deleted remote branches
git fetch --prune
```

## Collaboration Rules

### Before Starting Work
```bash
# Always pull latest
git checkout main
git pull origin main
```

### Communication
- **Small commits**: Easier to review
- **Clear messages**: Help teammates understand changes
- **Reference issues**: Link commits to tasks

### Code Review Etiquette
- **Review promptly** (within 24 hours)
- **Be constructive**: Suggest, don't demand
- **Test locally**: Pull and verify changes
- **Approve when ready**: Don't block unnecessarily

## Emergency Procedures

### Accidentally Committed Secrets
```bash
# 1. Immediately rotate the secret (API key, password)

# 2. Remove from latest commit
git reset --soft HEAD~1
git restore --staged .env

# 3. Recommit without secret
git add .
git commit -m "feat: Add new feature"

# 4. Force push (if already pushed)
git push origin main --force

# 5. Consider using git-filter-branch for older commits
```

### Accidentally Deleted Files
```bash
# Restore from last commit
git checkout HEAD agent.py

# Restore from specific commit
git checkout <commit-hash> agent.py
```

### Need to Revert to Earlier State
```bash
# View commit history
git log --oneline

# Revert to specific commit
git revert <commit-hash>

# Or reset (dangerous, rewrites history)
git reset --hard <commit-hash>
```

